WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.830
Speaker 1: I want to start today by talking
about President Joe Biden's upcoming Supreme

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:05.830
Court pick.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:11.180
As many of you have no doubt heard by now,
the oldest liberal justice on the court, Stephen

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:17.620
Breyer is going to be retiring and Joe Biden
is going to get to pick or nominate rather

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.530
a replacement, which is subject to confirmation
by the Senate now.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:26.230
Joe Biden made a promise during the campaign
that he would select a black woman, which

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:32.640
would be, if confirmed, the first black woman
ever on the United States Supreme Court.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.579
He confirmed that that's still the plan.

00:00:34.579 --> 00:00:38.670
Jen Psaki, his White House press secretary,
confirmed it, and I believe Joe Biden has

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:42.410
also been asked about it and confirmed that
as well.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:51.510
The American Right is now starting a campaign
to make the case that this is extremely discriminatory

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:56.729
and essentially racist to anyone who is not
a black woman.

00:00:56.729 --> 00:01:00.429
In other words, the way that many are framing
it and we're going to look at Laura Ingram

00:01:00.429 --> 00:01:07.320
in a moment, who's doing this is if you are
excluding anyone who is not a black woman,

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:14.630
it is by definition, discriminatory and or
racist against those individuals.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.180
This is wacky.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:21.479
And as someone who is not a woke stir and
not into corrosive identity politics, I'm

00:01:21.479 --> 00:01:24.119
going to explain to you why these people are
wrong.

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:25.799
But let's first listen to Laura Ingraham.

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:30.530
Speaker 2: Like everything else, Joe Biden
touches his Supreme Court selection process

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:31.530
is in shambles.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:37.310
Candidate Biden, he thought he was being really
woke and so cool by pledging to nominate an

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.340
African-American woman to the High Court.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:45.700
But of course, he was also effectively discriminating
against a vast majority of the adult population.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:51.399
Oh, and now even liberal websites like Slate
thinks he has himself in a bind, claiming

00:01:51.399 --> 00:01:56.049
that Biden's pledge has backfired and needlessly
tokenized future nominees.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:02:01.909
Speaker 1: So let me remind you, I am not
an identity politics guy.

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:13.250
I have spoken out for a decade about uses
of identity to silence or to exclude you all.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.470
You've been watching this show listening to
my podcast for a while.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.680
You know that.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.060
Let's go through this now in that context,
in steps.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:26.500
First of all, is what Joe Biden is doing unique.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.920
And the answer is no, it is not.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:35.100
Here is Donald Trump saying I'm choosing between
women only for this next scene and the crowd

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.100
cheered Greene.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:39.720
Speaker 3: I will be putting forth a nominee
next week.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.560
It will be a woman.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.270
Speaker 1: Right?

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:46.540
It wasn't only Donald Trump who did this.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.060
Ronald Reagan did the exact same thing.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:52.870
Speaker 3: Polls continuing to show he runs
better among men than women.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:56.110
Reagan took a dramatic step today to reach
out for female support.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:01.970
Now I'm announcing today that one of the first
Supreme Court vacancies in my administration

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:05.180
will be filled by the most qualified woman
I can possibly find.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.610
Speaker 1: Oh whoa, hold on a second.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:11.340
Now you can say, Well, they were all wrong
to do that, David.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.910
OK, fine, you could take that position.

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:19.960
But were you actually saying it at the time
or are you saying it now that they already

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:25.240
put women on the courts and you no longer
really have to say anything about it?

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:26.880
It's very easy now to say, Well, they were
all wrong.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.790
None of them should have done it, but that's
not really the most important thing to think

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:30.790
about.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:33.720
I'm putting for context that this is not unique.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:37.880
So a lot of the criticism of Biden is hypocritical,
but the most important thing is the context

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:39.510
that matters here.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:47.750
The Supreme Court was established in 1789,
from 1789 until 1967.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:50.630
That's 178 years.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:55.950
Every single justice was white and male.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:04:02.070
OK, one hundred and seventy eight years and
during that time, we had slavery in the United

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:06.310
States for roughly 80 years of that 178 years.

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:11.130
We had slavery of black people and an all
white male court.

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:12.720
So it's OK.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:17.820
And it's notable when we say, Hey, we now
have a black person on the court, which came

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.370
in 1967 with Thurgood Marshall.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:22.019
It's not racist.

00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:23.520
It's not discriminatory.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:27.350
It's look at the makeup of the country and
look at the makeup of the court.

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:31.040
And at this point, with so many qualified
black jurists, how have we not had one?

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.290
It's OK to point that out.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:36.380
You're not participating in toxic and corrosive
identity politics.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:40.940
Let's give another example from 1789 until
1981.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:42.500
We had all men on the court.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:45.240
That's one hundred and ninety two years.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.660
Every single justice was a man.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:49.660
So it's OK.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:57.520
And notable to say, given the history of qualified
women lawyers, judges, here's finally the

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:58.520
first.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:04.810
The woman on the court when Sandra Day O'Connor
was nominated to the court, there has never

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:07.600
been an Asian person on the Supreme Court.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:12.070
Native American, Pacific Islander, black woman,
Indian-American, etc.

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:18.300
We don't need a court that exactly matches
the makeup of the U.S. in every turn, every

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.830
every sort of demographic characteristic.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:23.840
Nor is it even possible with only nine people
on the court.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:27.340
But at a certain point when you say, Wow,
we have 330 million people in the country

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.700
now, the Supreme Court's been around more
than 200 years.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:37.389
It starts to get weird that we have not had
certain people on the court.

00:05:37.389 --> 00:05:42.040
Now they start to play its identity over qualifications.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:48.790
They say we're ignoring who are the most qualified
people because we're focused on identity instead

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:50.250
of qualifications.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.340
And again, that's a terrible argument.

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:56.840
Once again, we're a country of three hundred
and thirty one million people.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:04.230
If I were to say or if Joe Biden were to say,
I am going to pick the first former sports,

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:10.020
oh OK, current or former sports team owner
who is a woman, we would say, Wow, that's

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.230
like a really small group.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:14.360
There's not a lot of female major sports team
owners.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:17.639
It's like, you know, Renee Montgomery and
Michelle Williams from Destiny's Child as

00:06:17.639 --> 00:06:21.810
a part owner of a team and Jeanie Buss owns
parts of multiple NBA teams.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.290
We might be saying that's really weird.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:31.960
That identity designation is not appealing
to appearing to be a pool of qualified people.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:37.960
Joe Biden is picking one black woman, and
there are many qualified black women.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:43.950
There is no reason to believe that by saying
I'm going to pick a black woman and it's going

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:48.230
to be notable, given the history of the country
in the history of the court, there's no reason

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:51.400
to believe that it's going to be a less qualified
individual.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:56.169
You're picking from among the many qualified
black women.

00:06:56.169 --> 00:07:03.290
It is such a non-story, and that's me as a
non woke non identity person, not identity

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:07.490
politics person telling you this, but they're
going to keep playing it up and they're going

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:09.669
to make it into something that it is not.

00:07:09.669 --> 00:07:32.010
If you disagree with me, I would love to hear
from you.

00:07:32.010 --> 00:08:13.789
Respectfully, of course.

